# CORRIGENDUM to the retained log gen_fu_l36_dbg_driver_livelock.log (landing 36, committed 1deec4c).
# The retained log is NOT edited. This answers OR-36-1 and CM212 Low-1, Low-2 and Info-3.
#
# OR-36-1 and CM212-Low-1: THE BUILDS. The retained log named the failing run's build (head-mode at 962d31f) and
# called the others "one root" and "the fixed root". All three local runs are named here, each with the root's git
# head and the sha256 of the three SystemVerilog files the fix changes, on both sides of the change. Two of the three
# runs changed only a Python bound, and the identical hashes below are the evidence for that rather than a claim.
#   local reproduction and the sixteenfold-bound run   root: a detached archive of 962d31f
#   the fixed-driver run                               root: a detached archive of b105c09
# The digest each root's compile reports is the LOCAL runner's find-digest over dv/auto_dv env, tb, isa and gen_tb,
# written by gen_tb_local.sh line 37 into config_opts.txt under the key "sources sha256 (dv/auto_dv env, tb, isa,
# gen_tb)". It is NOT the committer's gate digest, which is gen_flow_util.filelist_digest over gen_rtl.f plus
# gen_tb.f. NO COMMITTED GATE IDENTITY APPLIES to any of these roots and none is claimed: the fixed root is b105c09
# plus three files, while the landing committed a different tree at 1deec4c.
# THE LINK THAT MATTERS, stronger than any digest of a scratch root: the three overlaid files are byte-identical to
# the blobs the landing committed, compared per file below, so the green half of the red ran on the bytes that landed.
#
# CM212-Low-2: A CLAIM WITH NOTHING UNDER IT, corrected. Section 1 of the retained log reads "Zero UVM_ERROR and zero
# UVM_FATAL: the log's own severity counts read" and is then followed by BLANK LINES, at its lines 43-44, 73 and 80.
# The reason is in section 3 of the same log: the cocotb assertion aborts the test before the UVM report phase, so a
# failing run has no severity summary at all and the grep that was to quote it matched nothing. The log therefore
# stated the reason in one place and asserted the counts in another, which is the defect. THE MEASURED POSITION:
# both committed-driver runs have ZERO severity lines and no UVM report summary; the FIXED run has both, reading
# UVM_ERROR : 0 and UVM_FATAL : 0. The zero-error claim is true of the fixed run and is unsupported for the failing
# runs, where the correct statement is that no checker verdict exists because the report phase never ran. What does
# stand for the failing runs is the cocotb assertion text and the record-stream evidence, neither of which needs the
# report phase.
# ALSO CM212-Low-2: the retained log's closing line says every figure is read "by the command printed above it".
# That holds for the section-1 measurement block and NOT for the whole log: sections 2, 3 and 4 quote figures from
# scripts whose commands are not reproduced line by line beside them. The claim is scoped here to the block it
# describes.
#
# CM212-Info-3: THE LEVEL LAGS ON EXIT AS WELL AS ON ENTRY, and the consequence differs. The retained log records the
# entry lag, that the level is derived from retired records so a release can be a few cycles late. The same lag
# applies leaving debug mode: after a dret the core is out while the level still reads high until a non-debug record
# retires, so a request asserted inside that window sees the level high and is released at once, giving a ONE-CYCLE
# PULSE instead of a hold until the next entry. That is narrower stimulus than the policy intends, not a hang, and it
# is the price of deriving the level from the record stream rather than from a DUT-boundary signal.

